Harden Gambatte's two-byte Game Link protocol for handheld Wi-Fi.

- Add TCP_NODELAY so Nagle/delayed-ACK interaction cannot inflate each
  request/reply exchange.
- Use deadline-bound complete reads/writes instead of assuming one syscall
  transfers both bytes.
- Do not restart Game Link for unrelated frontend option changes.
- Allow immediate server rebinding after a real configuration change.
- Log ten-second exchange latency summaries for device diagnosis.
- Give the hardened wire behavior a distinct version so an old and new core
  cannot be negotiated as compatible merely because they share an upstream
  commit.

